  "note": "Poses: the body frame's origin is the left imager's optical centre, which the datasheet names as the depth origin (section 4.8.1, \"the X-Y center of the left imager\"); the right imager sits one baseline along -y (the left imager is on the left looking out, section 3.6.1). Both optical axes are taken as parallel to body x (the rectified stereo geometry the depth output uses); the units' own extrinsics come from calibration. The RGB camera is \"not integrated in the module\" (Table 2-2) and neither source states its offset from the left imager: it is placed at the depth origin as an ASSUMPTION (pose_stated false); the RGB lens's f-number and focus are not stated. Not stated by the maker: pixel size (no table gives it), lens distortion coefficients (the datasheet gives only \"Distortion <= 1.5%\"), the stereo matcher's subpixel accuracy. The lens model is therefore pinhole (a labelled assumption); calibrate a unit for its own K and D. The FOVs vary unit to unit by about +/-3 degrees (mechanical tolerance +/-5%, datasheet Table 3-49 note 3). max_range_m is the upper figure of the datasheet's \"Range\" feature line, which reads \"over\" that figure and \"varies with lighting conditions\" (depth.range_text). Stream modes are the USB 3.1 Gen 1 tables; the USB 2.0 tables (fewer modes) are not entered. power_w is the datasheet's \"All Components\" power at its Max Operating Mode (section 7.4), not a measured average. The datasheet's RGB sensor is an OmniVision OV2740 (Table 3-49) and the stereo imagers OV9282 (module D430, Table 3-13). The store page gives min-Z \"~28 cm\" at max resolution, which matches the datasheet table (280 mm at 1280x720); the feature line reads \"Range 0.2 m to over 3 m\", the store page \"Ideal Range .3 m to 3 m\". Depth accuracy: datasheet Z-accuracy +/-2% (<= 2 m, 80% ROI, HD), store page \"<2% at 2 m\". The D435i adds a 6-DoF IMU (Table 3-49; BMI055 or BMI085 by SKU, Table 3-56 product codes); the IMU is not modelled here. Its power, size and mass rows are the D43x ones (Tables 3-52 and 7-8). The projector's position between the imagers is drawn in the datasheet (Figures 3-4 to 3-6) but no offset is given: it is placed at the baseline midpoint as an ASSUMPTION (pose_stated false); its FOV is the datasheet's.",
